# pooling ci — three dtypes x the algorithm and parameter families
#
# Shape column = the case's view: MxNxK with M = mb*OH, N = OW, K = 1;
# the params column carries the algorithm name (max | avg | avgex; default
# max) and the geometry in the fixed key order mb,ic,ih,iw,kh,kw
# [,sh,sw][,pt,pb,pl,pr] (see tests/inputs/README.md). The pad families
# cover windows that overhang the input on either side, the boundary case
# of avg_exclude where the in-bounds count drops below KH*KW.
#
# Families covered: k2s2, k3s2p1, asymmetric pad, non-square kernel/stride,
# the k=1xIW full-window row, kh=ih (window spans the whole height), mb>1,
# ragged channel counts, a 1x1 input, the empty-window family (pad >= k: max
# returns -FLT_MAX; the h case is vertically empty, the w case has an empty
# prefix of lanes across a strip), and the exclude-corner family.
#
# f32 is bit-exact against the scalar golden; f16/bf16 compare at the dtype
# trait tolerance.
